course: dictionary
lesson: 7132
title: Penguins and the cold
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A penguin is a black-and-white sea bird that cannot fly. Its body and its life are shaped by the cold. Read the words around the word to see how. «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» The clues are thick layer, fat and warm, so a penguin is built to stay warm in cold places.
explain: Penguins live mostly in the cold far south. The clue is in the sentence about emperor penguins: «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands.» To huddle means to crowd close together to keep warm, so the penguins share their heat.
explain: Check a meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Leopard seals are big hunters that catch penguins.» Penguin must be an animal, because a seal can catch it and eat it. Penguins are birds, so they have feathers and lay eggs, but they swim like fish, using their wings as flippers.
fact: A penguin is a black-and-white sea bird that cannot fly.
fact: Penguins swim very well and use their wings as flippers.
fact: Most penguins live in the cold far south, in the Southern Hemisphere, not at the North Pole.
fact: Emperor penguin fathers keep the egg warm on their feet, under a fold of belly skin.
fact: A group of penguins living together is called «a colony of penguins».
exercise: «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» How do penguins keep warm? | By flying south every winter | By sitting in the hot sun | *With thick fat and tightly packed feathers | By swimming in warm water
exercise: Where do most penguins live? | At the North Pole | In the middle of a city | In hot deserts | *In the cold far south
exercise: «Leopard seals are big hunters with powerful jaws that catch penguins.» What do leopard seals do to penguins? | Count them | *Catch them | Keep them warm | Teach them to swim
test: «Emperor penguin fathers keep the egg warm on their feet.» What do emperor penguin fathers use to keep the egg warm? | A hot stone | Their wings | Their beaks | *Their feet
test: A penguin cannot fly. What does it use its wings for in the sea? | *As flippers to swim | To wave to friends | To keep the sun off | To fly over the ice
exam: Penguins are birds that cannot fly. Which fact about them is true? | They have no feathers and do not lay eggs | They live in hot deserts and never swim | *They live mostly in the cold far south | They fly to the North Pole every winter
